  "known_limitations": [
    "FAERS holds spontaneous reports. Disproportionality finds reporting patterns; it cannot show causation, incidence or relative risk in patients.",
    "The signal benchmark's outcome definitions (MedDRA Preferred Terms per outcome) are a draft that no clinical reviewer has signed off.",
    "The OMOP reference set's negative controls are imperfect; a published audit found a substantial share (about 17%) may be misclassified.",
    "The EU-ADR copy used has 93 pairs; the original paper reports 94.",
    "Interaction-model test sets use sampled negatives (unlabelled pairs, not confirmed non-interactions) at a 1:1 ratio, so precision at k is read against a base rate of 0.5.",
    "NER precision is a lower bound: the ADE corpus annotates only entities in annotated relations.",
    "NER results come from published case-report text, not from prescriptions or social media.",
    "Prescription extraction was measured on synthetic printed documents. Handwriting is untested, and brand names missing from FAERS (for example many Indian brands) are not recognised; they are flagged for checking.",
    "The lead-time study compares FAERS signals with FDA label changes over only 20 quarters; reporting rises after label changes, FAERS dates are receipt dates, and the label-change reference maps label text to Preferred Terms automatically and is pending faculty review."
  ]
